.nh
.TH "PB-PREVIEW-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-preview-list - List temporary previews


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb preview list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List temporary previews

.PP
List account-visible temporary previews and their state. Select an exact preview identity for status, inspect, replay, stop, or delete.

.PP
A preview exposes a local target through a temporary Paperboat URL or private/team access policy. Inspect its status before sharing the URL, and stop or delete it when no longer needed. Browser HTTP terminates TLS at the edge.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--cursor\fP=""
	continue a previous page

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical preview resources as JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=100
	maximum results (1-200)

.PP
\fB--owner\fP=""
	filter owner: mine, shared, or an authorized account ID

.PP
\fB--q\fP=""
	filter by resource name or ID

.PP
\fB--state\fP=""
	filter by resource state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-preview(1)\fP
